h K or V row from 25,728\n  to 24,704 bytes, with bit-exact raw-secondary fallback for arbitrary\n  exception overflow instead of a sample-dependent correctness assumption;\n- optional cached intra-layer H2D/decode pipelining, enabled explicitly with\n  `TIERED_SERVE_KV_CD3_PIPELINE_CHUNK_BLOCKS=1024` from 1,536 active blocks,\n  with an automatic single-copy fallback for highly fragmented slot sets;\n- serving-suite codec selection through `--codecs p4flat,cd3`, including\n  codec-specific weight/KV arguments, configs, result labels and manifests;\n- a fully CPU P4Flat weight post-process (blocked relayout and subtile codec),\n  so CPU weight encoding no longer launches CUDA encode kernels;\n- a frozen-split weight benchmark that separately reports H2D, resident GPU\n  decode, and their combined latency.\n- projection-specific fused-N calibration overrides, with a uniform override\n  retained for compatibility;\n- exact-length CD3 frozen-split staging views, so standalone fallback accepts\n  variable-sized Packed20x3 exception streams;\n- startup route reporting that reflects projection-specific overrides.\n- a GH200/Llama-70B prefill weight-stream cutoff of N=1856: compressed\n  standalone decode below the cutoff and raw BF16 transfer at or above it;\n- an AST-level regression test that pins the calibrated CD3 cutoff.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The old CD3 patch's complete path set is contained in this patch.\n- Applied cleanly after startup prerequisites on source HEAD.\n- All 33 restored tiered-serve files matched the selected live files\n  byte-for-byte.\n- `git diff --check`, Python byte compilation, and shell syntax checks passed.\n- The consolidated patch applied after both startup prerequisites in a clean\n  worktree and all 32 restored files matched the live files byte-for-byte.\n- The vLLM integration patch reverse-checks against the validated live tree.\n- 33 CD3, prefill weight-stream, and KV-prefill policy tests passed.\n- The current CD3 test file passes all 20 tests, including compact-row planner\n  agreement, forced exception overflow, slot reuse, and one/two-stream decode.\n- The renamed `chunk_delta3_ext` built and imported successfully.\n- Synthetic CPU weight encode/GPU decode, CPU KV encode, and KV H2D+decode\n  smoke benchmarks were bit-exact.\n- Offline suite smoke (`cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp`, batches 64/128, input 1020,\n  output 2) completed successfully with the compact planner and restored a\n  clean GPU/hugepage boundary.\n- Online suite smoke (`cd3`, `kvcomp`, chunk 64, two requests) completed with\n  2/2 successful requests, 4,455 input tokens, 118 output tokens, and a clean\n  GPU/hugepage boundary. The serving suite now exposes `--smoke`; normal suite\n  defaults remain unchanged.\n- The offline suite now includes a non-fused `cao-cd3` cell and a\n  `--breakdown` switch that forwards `--time-breakdown` to every selected\n  method. A three-method/five-batch dry-run verified the non-fused, fused, and\n  fused+KV-compression command separation.\n- Actual Llama-3.1-70B weight round-trip: qkv/o/gateup/down all bit-exact.\n- Layer-40 CD3 CPU weight encode median total: 130.7 ms, versus P4Flat CPU\n  1951.9 ms (about 14.9x faster); compression ratio about 1.368x versus 1.326x.\n- GH200 CPU KV encode median with one serving worker, K+V: N=8 0.16 ms;\n  N=64 0.27 ms; N=128 0.37 ms; N=256 0.47 ms; N=1024 0.99 ms;\n  N=2048 2.02 ms. All cases were bit-exact.\n- Full serving initialization installed all 320 fused Linear overrides and\n  completed all 320 CPU-compressed weight cells.\n- Layer-40 standalone weight decode median gained another 1.4% in aggregate\n  from half-width live output accumulation (all four groups bit-exact).\n- Resident production KV decode improved 1.69x--2.04x for N=8/64/256 by\n  writing directly to the final cache. Partial H2D restore at high-water=1024\n  improved 16% for N=64 and 12% for N=256.\n- Final current-stride standalone K+V H2D+decode medians for CD3 are\n  0.044/0.043/0.077/0.226/0.413/0.786/1.130 ms at\n  N=8/64/256/1024/2048/4096/6000 versus P4Flat\n  0.062/0.066/0.092/0.250/0.452/0.858/1.232 ms, making CD3\n  28.6/34.3/16.4/9.7/8.7/8.4/8.3% faster.\n- With the optional serving-style separate load/decode pipeline at N=6000,\n  cached\n  intra-layer pipelining reduces CD3 from 1.115 to 0.963 ms and beats P4Flat's\n  1.214 ms by 20.7%; N=1536 improves from 0.309 to 0.280 ms. All outputs were\n  bit-exact. The N=6000 scaling case cycles the 4,096 saved real KV blocks.\n- A 16-layer CD3 pipeline gains 30.3% at N=256 and 25.8% at N=1024 from\n  H2D/decode overlap; all cases remained bit-exact.\n- CPU-encoded production KV H2D+decode steady-state median on GH200 is\n  0.065/0.065/0.102/0.251 ms for N=8/64/256/1024. P4Flat under the same\n  split-measurement run is 0.063/0.070/0.107/0.302 ms. CD3 resident decode is\n  0.028/0.029/0.036/0.065 ms versus P4Flat 0.046/0.047/0.049/0.082 ms; CD3\n  H2D is 0.016/0.026/0.056/0.173 ms versus 0.030/0.042/0.081/0.232 ms.\n  The pre-blob CD3 values were\n  0.247/0.291/0.374/0.762 ms; all cases were bit-exact. This historical P4Flat\n  comparison used its raw-safe 32,768-byte blob stride. Current P4Flat defaults\n  to a 25,600-byte tight stride, so these P4Flat values must not be used as the\n  final current-codec comparison.\n- Layer-40 frozen-split weight medians on GH200 (qkv/o/gateup/down summed):\n  CD3 H2D 1.200 ms, resident decode 0.923 ms, H2D+decode 2.127 ms; P4Flat\n  H2D 1.353 ms, resident decode 0.906 ms, H2D+decode 2.232 ms. CD3 therefore\n  transfers 11.3% faster and finishes the production pair 4.7% faster while\n  its isolated decode is 1.9% slower. All four weights were bit-exact.\n- Rejected experiments are not present: warp-owner exception pre-application\n  was about 2.3x slower, pairwise 3xU32 code loading was neutral/regressive,\n  64-thread or register-forced 10-CTA kernels were 7--12% slower, and a\n  separate standalone exception kernel was 50.7% slower than integrated patch.\n- Fused route calibration with concurrent H2D found all four projections faster\n  for every tested N=65..128. At N=129 the Npad=192 transition makes fused\n  about 1.6--1.7x slower, so the production cutoff is exactly 128.\n- An all-80-layer QKV sweep found fused wins on 79/80 layers and saves\n  0.508/0.595/1.211 ms in aggregate at N=80/96/128. The exception-heavy layer\n  0 is the sole loser. End-to-end TPOT P50 for all-fused versus QKV-standalone\n  was 171.90/188.40/219.26 versus 172.20/187.96/219.30 ms at batch\n  80/96/128, confirming a tie at engine level and favoring all-fused because it\n  avoids dense-weight HBM writes.\n- End-to-end forced-route prefill sweeps placed the standalone/raw crossover\n  between N=1824 and N=1856. At N=1824 standalone led by 18.630 ms; at N=1856\n  raw led by 20.405 ms, and raw remained ahead through N=3072. An unforced run\n  confirmed standalone routing at N=1792/1824 and raw routing at N=1856/1888.\n  The full report and source logs are stored under\n  `/lambda/nfs/whchoi/experiment-results/cd3-20260901-route/`.\n- Final whole-engine Llama-70B TPOT median is 114.51 ms versus P4Flat\n  124.66 ms at batch 64 (8.14% faster), and 166.64 versus 180.59 ms at batch\n  128 (7.72% faster). Both methods used CPU weight/KV encode and production\n  GPU decode/fused routing.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788356693167,"completed_at_ms":1788356693239}}
